meta {
  name: Delete my account
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/account
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Deletes the auth user, the profile, and everything that cascades from it:
  games, play sessions, wishlist, follow edges. `rate_limits` has no FK to
  `profiles`, so those rows are deleted explicitly.

  Idempotent, for the same reason follow and unfollow are: a repeat on a
  still-valid token for an already-deleted account is 204, not an error. It also
  succeeds for a caller who never onboarded, since the auth user is theirs and
  still deletable.

  Destructive and unconfirmable. Point this at a local test account only.

  - 204 deleted
  - 403 the founder's account, which the rest of the site depends on
  - 503 the accounts service was unreachable; nothing was deleted
}
